+- **Study 1** has small samples; the key Sonnet relay comparison is not significant. Protocols can limit assembly on their own. Framing changes several cues together, and relay wording differs from other conditions. We test no network-shape variations, swarms above four agents, compromised-agent spread or real swarm traces.
+- **Study 2** uses one model and one fixed pipeline, without second-model replication. Metadata is trusted. The monitor changes information, call count and veto power together. Zero events in 50 trials still permits a one-sided 95% upper bound of about 5.8% on a common failure probability, assuming independent identically distributed Bernoulli trials [clopper1934confidence].
 
