+### 6.4 Completion and validation status
+
+Study 1 contains all 1,040 planned and rerun rows, with 7,670 logged calls and no recorded failures. Study 2 contains all 800 planned trial keys across 16 cells; 799 are valid. Its one backend failure was excluded without replacement, as the protocol required. Offline replays reproduce the recorded analyses. These checks establish internal reproducibility, not independent replication of model behavior or broad validation of the shared hypothesis.
+
 ## 7 Conclusion
 
-In this synthetic task, explicitly naming the restricted goal was associated with refusal in the measured solo trials; a split did not establish a general safety failure. In Study 1, a split that hid the goal from every agent sometimes produced the restricted artifact (requested Sonnet: 7 of 30 relays, 4 of 10 seeds; one pooled cell had mixed served models, and the verified-model rerun gave 1 of 10), though less often than a single agent kept equally uninformed. In Study 2, no restricted recoverability was observed under trusted provenance on the sampled held-out seeds, while authorized work improved, where a keyword gate and an LLM monitor failed. Evaluations of agent systems should test what each agent learns about the goal, not only whether it refuses. Next steps: second-model and cross-provider replications, more relay seeds, wording sweeps, forged-provenance tests, asynchronous swarms with tools, and the unimplemented [sender-level SAE intervention](../docs/protocols/sae-sender-study-proposal.md).
+Study 1 finds a framing effect and recoverability across posts, without establishing greater assembly from dividing work. Study 2 finds that trusted task purpose improves restricted-disclosure and authorized-completion outcomes in one pipeline. Evaluations should therefore measure purpose information, aggregate disclosure and useful completion together.
+
+Independent model/provider replication, more relay seeds with a six-call solo baseline, varied wording, forged metadata and larger asynchronous swarms remain future work. The proposed [sender-level SAE intervention](../docs/protocols/sae-sender-study-proposal.md) is unimplemented.
 
